.TH MPVR 1 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mpvr \- play desktop and stereoscopic XR video with mpv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
mpvr [XR\-OPTIONS] [MPV\-OPTIONS] [FILE...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A native mpv fork and Python launcher for GPU side\-by\-side playback in DomeD or an active WiVRn/WayVR session. Existing SBS content is fitted per eye, with subtitles duplicated. No depth synthesis is performed. In automatic mode outside DomeD, unrecognized or mono video stays on the desktop; DomeD can duplicate mono content into both eyes. Unrecognized options are passed to mpv.
.PP
Decoding, audio, synchronization, seeking and GPU rendering remain in mpv.
The interface uses mpv/Lua rather than FLTK or Qt; DE_XR_TOOLKIT has no effect.
Top/bottom input is repacked to SBS on the GPU. Unsupported spherical,
checkerboard, interleaved and anaglyph sources are not depth-converted.
.SH ROUTING
Auto stays with a verified DomeD session when present; an inactive/incompatible
DomeD falls back to ordinary desktop playback. Outside DomeD, connected WiVRn/WayVR
is selected only for recognized stereo sources. Unverified/mono video stays
on the desktop, including a requested WayVR route without an explicit stereo layout.
Explicit stereo XR requests fail if the selected backend is unavailable.
No desktop, runtime or headset session is started or restarted by this launcher.
.PP
Stream metadata takes precedence over filename packing markers; an explicit
layout overrides detection. A wide image or a bare 3D label is insufficient.
Full/half SBS and top/bottom markers are supported, including right-first order.
Opaque webpage URLs outside DomeD need a manual layout to route to WayVR;
mpv's yt-dlp hook resolves the media rather than a second launcher extraction.
Inside DomeD unknown sources can duplicate mono into both eyes.
.PP
Loading unrecognized/2D content later in WayVR pauses/blacks the transport and
hands that content to a normal desktop player, preserving position, volume,
mute and speed. The remaining XR playlist is not resumed after that handoff.
.SH APPLICATION MENU
The application-menu entry uses \-\-player-operation-mode=pseudo-gui. With no
file selected it opens an idle desktop window, including when DomeD or XR is
active. Drop media into that window to begin playback. The player exits after
the playlist finishes. Ordinary command-line invocation retains mpv behavior;
use the pseudo-gui option explicitly when an idle window is wanted.
.PP
On Wayland, builds with GIO export the live player menu through KDE AppMenu and
DBusMenu to DomeD's universal menu bar. Playback, tracks, audio, subtitles and
window commands follow the existing context menu and custom menu.conf definitions,
including nested menus, shortcuts and live checked, hidden and disabled states.
Top-level actions appear under Player. Each window owns its export, which is
removed when the window closes. The ordinary context menu remains available
when the compositor or session bus does not support application menus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-xr\-help"
Show launcher\-specific help. \-\-help shows mpv help.
.TP
.B "\-\-xr\-output auto|wayvr|domed|desktop|off"
Select output routing; default auto. desktop is a squeezed SBS transport
preview, while off keeps ordinary upstream desktop playback.
.TP
.B "\-\-domed"
Select the DomeD backend.
.TP
.B "\-\-sbs\-layout auto|full\-sbs|half\-sbs|full\-tb|half\-tb|mono"
Override stereo layout detection. Full/half top-bottom input is repacked to SBS on the GPU.
.TP
.B "\-\-swap\-eyes"
Swap the left and right views.
.TP
.B "\-\-xr\-size WIDTHxHEIGHT"
Select XR transport resolution; default 2560x1440. Dimensions must be 10 to
9999 pixels and width must be even. This is not a per-eye resolution option.
.SH CONTROLS
Standard mpv controls remain: Space pauses, arrows seek and q quits.
Desktop right-click opens the context menu, Ctrl+P opens the menu and the
backtick key opens the console. XR output duplicates OSD/subtitles and retains
keyboard controls; the ordinary mouse OSC is disabled on the packed stereo surface.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MPVR_NATIVE_PLAYER
Override the compiled mpv executable used by the launcher and render tests.
.TP
.B MPVR_WAYVRCTL
Override the WayVR control executable.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Select the compositor socket/runtime directory. DomeD discovery verifies the
same-user socket peer and owned session record before selecting its XR socket.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Depth synthesis is not provided. Avoid additional crop/rotate/stereo pixel
filters in XR mode. HDR depends on mpv and the compositor/runtime; SDR tests
do not validate HDR or sustained physical-headset playback.
.SH INSTALLATION
Build optimized mpv with its decoder/GPU/audio dependencies and Lua UI support.
The source xr/install.py helper takes --build-dir and installs per-user
launchers/assets, retaining backups under ~/.local/state/mpvr/backups.
It does not install this manual; copy it to the chosen prefix's share/man/man1.
It does not replace /usr/bin/mpv or the system libmpv.
.SH EXAMPLES
mpvr movie_SBS.mkv
.br
mpvr \-\-domed \-\-sbs\-layout=half\-sbs movie.mkv
.br
mpvr \-\-xr\-output=off movie.mkv
.br
mpvr \-\-sbs\-layout=full\-tb movie_FTB.mkv
.SH SEE ALSO
mpv(1), qimgvr(1), dome\-compositor(1)
